GL draws and uploads without Panfrost's CPU work and waits.

OutRun 2006 races on the RG DS (Mali-G52, Mesa 25.0):
- Each indexed draw passes its range: without it Mesa's u_vbuf scans the indices on the CPU, in write-combined
  memory, a quarter of the frame.
- Push buffers upload unsynchronized, each frame slot guarded by its own fence: glBufferSubData made Panfrost wait
  in panfrost_bo_wait for a third of the frame, with the emulation thread waiting behind it.

